cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sf-testimpact in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "sf-testimpact: change-impact analysis for safe Apex test selection in Salesforce deployments"
abstract: >-
  sf-testimpact performs static change-impact analysis for Salesforce. It builds a
  dependency graph of Apex and metadata, resolves a git diff into that graph, and
  computes the minimum set of Apex tests a change can affect, so a deployment runs only
  the relevant tests instead of the full suite. It is a correctness tool governed by the
  rule "over-approximate freely, under-approximate never": anything unresolvable widens
  the selection or falls back to running all tests, and reports the rule that fired.
type: software
